==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Rich Cat Sr.''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Richest Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Boasting pathetic stats, excluding his damage, Rich Cat III is mainly used for [[Cat Combo]]s he activates when he evolves ([[Itchy Riches (Combo)|Itchy Riches]] and [[Offshore Accounts (Combo)|Offshore Accounts]]). This turns him into a poor man's version of the [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] item, slightly speeding up the progress of the battle. This works very well on cash-tight stages, and can be combined with other similar combos for even greater effect, such as [[Longnecks (Combo)|Longnecks]] and [[Don't Mess With Me! (Combo)|Don't Mess With Me!]] Additionally, his strangely high attack power and increased money from defeating enemies can be used to kill peons at the beginning of a stage and rack up tons of money. However, Rich Cat III still has pathetic health and low range, so protect him with cheap meatshields if you use this strategy.

===True Form===
Richest Cat now can provide you higher attack power and one more combo to boot. His health and range are still lackluster, but his damage is enough to be a budgeted [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]. Although you would use the mentioned unit in battle due to her superior stats, Richest Cat remains as a decently good attacker.

